      "claim": "[18F]7a, a fluoroalkyl tetralin/piperidine sigma ligand, showed ~4% ID/g brain uptake in mice, indicating favorable brain penetration.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C05"],
      "claim": "PET in monkey showed rapid brain uptake of [18F]6FPWAY (4.33% ID), supporting CNS access for related fluoroaryl piperidine/piperazine ligands.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C06"],
      "claim": "AV-133, a fluoroethyl-tetralin-like ligand, gave brain/plasma ratios of 2.77-3.30 in rat, confirming ready brain access for this chemotype.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "A close CNS-penetrant analogue had a mouse brain/plasma ratio of 0.54 with no active efflux, supporting meaningful brain exposure for this structural class.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Pass. The query is a piperidine/tetralin fluoroalkyl ketone with strong structural analogy to sigma-receptor and CNS imaging ligands that consistently show high brain uptake across species; all high-transfer experimental records support meaningful CNS access.",
